id: finish-sign
name: Finish Sign
uaType: technical
prerequisite: Personality Score of 8+
tpCost: 15
type: standard
actionCost: 2
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
# "Declare a Signature Technique" - asked the first time, kept on the Item until it is used or released - and "gain a
# stack of 'Finisher' (max. 7)" each use (chat.mjs postFinishSign). Declared: no Energy Charge Maneuver; the Technique
# used, every stack an Energy Charge on it (use-maneuver.mjs, with what was charged); Mandatory Charge counts them
# (technique-use.mjs). Released as an Instant from its entry.
finishSign: true
resource: finisher
resourceMax: 7
resourceLabel: Finisher
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Declare a Signature Technique and gain a Finisher (max 7) each use; no Energy Charge Maneuver until the Technique is
  used, when every Finisher becomes an Energy Charge on it. Released as an Instant.
text: >
  Finish Sign: You are able to gather up power for an overwhelming attack under the guise of a cocky gesture.
  –Ability Type: Technical
  –Prerequisites: Personality Score of 8+
  –TP Cost: 15
  –KP Cost: 4(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard Maneuver
  –Action Cost: 2 Actions
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: Declare a Signature Technique. Until you use your declared Signature Technique, you cannot use the Energy
  Charge Maneuver, nor can you declare a different Signature Technique through the effects of Finish Sign.

  Each time you use Finish Sign with a declared Signature Technique (including the initial use of Finish Sign), gain a
  stack of ‘Finisher’ (max. 7). When you use your declared Signature Technique, you must convert all of your Finisher
  stacks into Energy Charges for that Signature Technique. Stacks of Finisher are considered to be uses of the Energy
  Charge Maneuver for the sake of the Mandatory Charge Disadvantage.

  As an Instant Maneuver, you can lose all stacks of Finisher, stop declaring your Signature Technique, and stop
  applying all effects of Finish Sign.
